[h1]0.9.2[/h1]

A bug-fix update led by the repair that matters most to current players: animal sales work now.

[hr][/hr]
[h1]Fixed[/h1]

[list]
[*][b]Animal sales now work.[/b] Marking an animal order ready used to do nothing, and one non-matching animal in a mixed flock could block the whole sale. Fixed and proven in play with both a chicken and a bonded labrador; the bond warning named the correct colonist.
[*][b]Signing fees are shown before you hire.[/b] The fee now appears when creating a job posting and beside every applicant, together with your current silver.
[*][b]Procurement quotes cannot be re-rolled.[/b] Withdrawing and repeating a request returns the same quotes until the market refreshes.
[*][b]Supplier stock is finite within a market window.[/b] Buying a supplier out and requesting again no longer restores their offer.
[*][b]Accepting one quote leaves the rest of the request open.[/b] Request 1,000 steel and buy 300, and the remaining 700 stays wanted with the other offers still available.
[*][b]Orders and deliveries use the correct colony.[/b] Buyer collection now refuses rather than taking goods from a colony that never offered them. Procurement deliveries and refunds fall back only when necessary, and say which colony received them.
[*][b]The mod reports its version at startup[/b], so bug reports can be tied to the build that produced them.
[/list]

[h1]Saves[/h1]

Saves from 0.9.0 and 0.9.1 upgrade automatically. The upgrade has been verified on a real existing save. Once upgraded, a save cannot be opened again by an older version of the mod.

[b]Keep a backup of any colony you care about before loading it with this pre-release.[/b]

Still a beta. Problems to the [url=https://github.com/miannoni/Intercolony/issues]GitHub issue tracker[/url], please, with your mod list and [b]Player.log[/b].
